.TH ZOSYAZI 1 "2026-11-19" "zosyazi 1.1.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zosyazi \- lightweight, Yazi-inspired terminal file manager for z/OS UNIX
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zosyazi.py
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zosyazi
is a zero-dependency Python 3 terminal file manager built for z/OS UNIX
(IBM Open Enterprise SDK for Python) using the standard \fBcurses\fR library.
It provides a three-column Miller layout (parent directory, current directory,
and live preview), Vim-style navigation, a built-in EBCDIC/ASCII-safe
full-screen file viewer, interactive \fBchtag\fR file tagging, JCL job
submission, Git branch and status badges, directory bookmarks, and native
z/OS \fB/dsfs\fR (Data Set File System) awareness.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I PATH
Initial directory, file, or \fB/dsfs\fR qualifier path to open (defaults to
the current working directory). Expands \fB~\fR and environment variables
(such as \fB$HOME\fR). If a file is specified, opens its parent directory
with that file highlighted. If a non-existent \fB/dsfs/<mode>/<hlq>/<qualifier>\fR
path is specified, opens \fB/dsfs/<mode>/<hlq>\fR with a strict prefix filter
(\fB<qualifier>.*\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-cwd\-file " FILE"
Write the final working directory to \fIFILE\fR on exit. Used by the shell
integration wrapper to change the parent shell's working directory on exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display the version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command-line usage help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ZOSYAZI_DSFS
Override the default DSFS mount point (default: \fB/dsfs\fR).
.TP
.B EDITOR
External editor launched when pressing \fBe\fR. If unset, \fBzosyazi\fR
prefers ASCII-native editors (\fBvim\fR, \fBnano\fR) over EBCDIC
\fB/bin/vi\fR to avoid garbling ASCII SSH terminals.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.SS Navigation
.TP
.BR j ", " Down
Move cursor down.
.TP
.BR k ", " Up
Move cursor up.
.TP
.BR h ", " H ", " Left ", " Backspace
Move up to parent directory (or select \fB..\fR and press Enter).
.TP
.BR l ", " Right ", " Enter
Enter directory or open file in the built-in viewer.
.TP
.B v
View current file in the built-in full-screen viewer.
.TP
.BR g ", " G
Jump to top or bottom of the directory list.
.TP
.B c
Change top-level path interactively (supports environment variables, \fB~\fR,
and \fB/dsfs\fR qualifier auto-filtering).
.TP
.B ~
Jump directly to the home directory.
.TP
.BR m \fI<key>\fR ", " ' \fI<key>\fR
Set or jump to a directory bookmark. Predefined bookmarks: \fBh\fR (home),
\fBr\fR (/), \fBt\fR (/tmp), \fBd\fR (/dsfs/txt).
.TP
.BR / ", " Esc
Filter current directory (\fBEsc\fR clears the active filter).
.TP
.B .
Toggle hidden dotfiles.
.SS File and z/OS Operations
.TP
.B Space
Toggle multi-select on the current item.
.TP
.BR y ", " x ", " p
Copy (yank), cut, or paste selected or highlighted items.
.TP
.B d
Delete selected or highlighted items (with confirmation).
.TP
.B r
Rename highlighted item.
.TP
.B a
Create a file (end the name with \fB/\fR to create a directory).
.TP
.B e
Open highlighted file in \fB$EDITOR\fR.
.TP
.B T
Interactive \fBchtag\fR z/OS file tagging (ISO8859-1, IBM-1047, UTF-8,
custom CCSID, or remove tag).
.TP
.BR ! ", " X
Execute a shell command (\fB%f\fR = filename, \fB%F\fR = full path) or
submit \fB.jcl\fR, \fB.cntl\fR, or \fB.job\fR files via \fB/bin/submit\fR.
.SS Built-In Viewer (v / Enter)
.TP
.BR j ", " k ", " Down ", " Up
Scroll down or up one line.
.TP
.BR PgDn ", " Space ", " PgUp ", " b
Scroll down or up one page.
.TP
.BR g ", " G
Jump to top or bottom of file.
.TP
.B e
Open current file in \fB$EDITOR\fR.
.TP
.B T
Manage z/OS file tag (\fBchtag\fR).
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc ", " h ", " Left
Return to directory view.
.SS General
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc
Quit \fBzosyazi\fR.
.TP
.BR F1 ", " ?
Open or close the colored, scrollable interactive tutorial.
.SH SHELL INTEGRATION
To automatically \fBcd\fR to the last browsed directory on exit, add the
following POSIX-compatible wrapper function to \fB~/.profile\fR,
\fB~/.bashrc\fR, or \fB~/.zshrc\fR:
.PP
.nf
yy() {
    _zosyazi_tmp="$(mktemp -t zosyazi-cwd.XXXXXX)"
    zosyazi.py --cwd-file="$_zosyazi_tmp" "$@"
    if [ -f "$_zosyazi_tmp" ]; then
        _zosyazi_dir="$(cat -- "$_zosyazi_tmp")"
        rm -f -- "$_zosyazi_tmp"
        if [ -n "$_zosyazi_dir" ] && [ -d "$_zosyazi_dir" ] && [ "$_zosyazi_dir" != "$PWD" ]; then
            cd -- "$_zosyazi_dir"
        fi
    fi
    unset _zosyazi_tmp _zosyazi_dir
}
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Open the current working directory:
.nf
    zosyazi.py
.fi
.PP
Open a specific directory or pre-select a file:
.nf
    zosyazi.py ~/projects/zosyazi
    zosyazi.py ~/.profile
.fi
.PP
Browse all MVS datasets under an HLQ in text mode:
.nf
    zosyazi.py /dsfs/txt/lbdyck
.fi
.PP
Auto-filter an HLQ to datasets starting with a qualifier (LBDYCK.TEST.*):
.nf
    zosyazi.py /dsfs/txt/lbdyck/test
.fi
.PP
Open a specific PDS directly to browse its members:
.nf
    zosyazi.py /dsfs/txt/lbdyck/test.pds
.fi
.PP
Inspect datasets in binary mode (Hex + ASCII preview and viewer):
.nf
    zosyazi.py /dsfs/bin/lbdyck
.fi
.PP
Launch with shell cd-on-exit integration:
.nf
    yy /dsfs/txt/lbdyck
.fi
